Example 1.2: A motor cyclist (to be treated as a point mass) is to undertake horizontal circles inside the cylindrical wall of a well of inner radius 4 m. Coefficient of static friction between the tyres and the wall is 0.4. Calculate the minimum speed and frequency necessary to perform this stunt. (Use g = 10 \text{ m/s}^2)
Solution:
v_{min} = \sqrt{\frac{rg}{\mu_s}} = \sqrt{\frac{4 \times 10}{0.4}} = 10 \text{ m s}^{-1} \text{ and}
n_{min} = \frac{v_{min}}{2\pi r} = \frac{10}{2 \times \pi \times 4} \cong 0.4 \text{ rev s}^{-1}
1.3.3 Vehicle on a Banked Road:
